{"id":"chf-homes-by-size","title":"Bay Area nursing homes by size: complaints, substantiated findings, deficiencies and State citations, 2023 to 2026","question":"Set against its size, which of the case homes and the sold homes draws the most complaints, findings and State citations?","finding":"79 homes (42 case homes, 47 homes sold in 2019 to 2024, 10 both): 6,765 complaint and incident allegations in 2023 to 2025 by the site's count, from 5,011 distinct complaints and facility-reported incidents; 0.878 allegations per 1,000 resident days pooled (middle home 0.676); 533 complaints and incidents substantiated with deficiencies. Highest per resident day: Eden Healthcare Center (2.689; 346 allegations, 182 complaints and incidents, 13 substantiated); Herman Health Care Center (2.308; 241 allegations, 234 complaints and incidents, 16 substantiated); Bay Marina Post Acute (2.237; 217 allegations, 128 complaints and incidents, 22 substantiated). 166 State enforcement actions 2023 to 2026 to date, 23 of them class AA or A citations; 13 under appeal.","how":"Allegations: the site's own yearly counts of \"complaints and reported incidents\" (2023 to 2025), which equal the number of allegation rows in each home's complaint table at all 79 homes (one complaint can carry several allegations); distinct complaints and incidents are the distinct intake numbers. Substantiated: distinct intake numbers in the complaint table with at least one allegation \"Substantiated with deficiencies\". Deficiencies: the tags listed on every survey with findings, 2023 to 2026 to date. Citations and penalties: every row of the enforcement table, 2023 to 2026 to date, by the class first assessed; amounts first assessed. Beds are licensed beds in the State listing of 16 October 2026; resident days are the total patient days of each home's State financial reports for 2023, 2024 and 2025 (joined by the State financial-report number in the listing; homes without all three years have no rate). Nurse hours and federal citations at the harm or immediate-jeopardy level are from the October 2026 federal file (joined by the federal certification number). All joins are by exact identifiers.","limits":"A complaint is an allegation, and a home that reports its own incidents promptly scores higher. Homes for short-stay rehabilitation turn over more residents, and more residents bring more complaints. In 2025 the State moved to a new intake system whose rows do not use \"Unsubstantiated\", so only findings with deficiencies are compared. 2026 is to date. Appealed citations may be reduced or dismissed. Federal citation counts cover the federal file's own inspection cycles, not 2023 to 2026. The 79 homes are not a sample of the Bay Area: they are the homes two cases chose.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"home","t":"Nursing home","type":"org"},{"k":"city","t":"City","type":"text"},{"k":"role","t":"In the screen as","type":"text"},{"k":"beds","t":"Licensed beds","type":"int"},{"k":"residentDays","t":"Resident days, 2023-25","type":"int"},{"k":"complaints","t":"Complaint and incident allegations, 2023-25 (site count)","type":"int"},{"k":"perK","t":"Per 1,000 resident days","type":"times"},{"k":"perBed","t":"Per bed per year","type":"times"},{"k":"intakes3","t":"Distinct complaints and incidents","type":"int"},{"k":"intakePerK","t":"Per 1,000 resident days","type":"times"},{"k":"substantiated","t":"Substantiated with deficiencies","type":"int"},{"k":"subPerK","t":"Per 1,000 resident days","type":"times"},{"k":"tags","t":"Deficiency tags, 2023-26","type":"int"},{"k":"tagsPerBed","t":"Per bed","type":"times"},{"k":"aa","t":"Class AA citations","type":"int"},{"k":"a","t":"Class A","type":"int"},{"k":"b","t":"Class B","type":"int"},{"k":"staffingPenalties","t":"Nursing-hours penalties","type":"int"},{"k":"assessed","t":"Penalties first assessed","type":"usd"},{"k":"assessedPerBed","t":"Per bed","type":"usd"},{"k":"underAppeal","t":"Actions under appeal","type":"int"},{"k":"hours"